{
  "version": "2.17",
  "children": [
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "Zb3v5",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "Brief · Reglas y avisos",
      "width": 360,
      "fill": "$bg-muted",
      "cornerRadius": "$radius-md",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": "$space-4",
      "padding": "$space-5",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "sOker",
          "name": "BT",
          "fill": "$fg-default",
          "content": "Reglas y avisos — brief",
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 18,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "hBhm5",
          "name": "BB",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "The 'Reglas' tab plus the inbox behind the TopBar bell — reglas duras sin corazón, and everything the app decides to tell you.\n\nWhy one file: rules are only ONE of four notification producers (alert_triggered · earnings_reminder · maturity_reminder · system). The bandeja is where all four land, and the bell that opens it lives in the shared TopBar. Splitting them would re-vendor the kit for two screens.\n\nScreens: Reglas (Default · Vacío) · Nueva regla (sheet, D11 route-as-drawer) · Bandeja · Confluencia (D3, engine still design-only).\n\nBandeja/Vacío is deliberately NOT an artboard: it is the same layout with the list replaced by one line — a pure string swap belongs in the brief, not on canvas. Reglas/Vacío IS an artboard because it carries different content: suggested rules derived from what you already own.\n\nGrounding: alert_rules (condition enum of 9, threshold_value, window_days, cooldown_minutes default 60, status active/paused, last_triggered_at) · alert_events (message, triggered_at, event_status) · notifications (notification_type enum of 4, read/read_at, notifiable) · alert_preferences. Condition labels and the descriptive summary come verbatim from app/helpers/alerts_helper.rb.\n\n⚠ Two channels, not three (D16, corrected 2026-08-27). This brief used to ground on alert_preferences (browser_push, email_digest, sms_notifications). Read against db/schema.rb the table has exactly TWO booleans — email_digest and urgent_email. browser_push and its plumbing were deleted 2026-08-25 (#293) and sms_notifications never existed. The 'Avisos en la app' switch is gone from Cómo te aviso, and the block's footer stopped promising it: it now names the bandeja, which is real and is not a channel you toggle.\n\n⚠ Confluencia: the ledger's warning was half stale and half live, and both halves matter. STALE — 'el semáforo está diseñado, no construido' is false: lights 1 and 3 shipped and render at market/_confluence, reached from _analysis. LIVE — the code's own subtitle reads 'Tres señales, leídas por separado', which is the honest description of what it does: nothing combines them. The artboard promised 'cuando las tres se prenden dentro de la misma ventana' and drew a 'Ventana de confluencia · 5 días' control that nothing computes — the D13/D16/D25 pattern of a UI offering what the instance cannot do. The window keeps its artboard (design leads, D8) but now carries the same 'motor pendiente' treatment light 2 already had.\n\nLuz 3 no longer claims MACD. MACD exists only as a 20%-weighted factor inside TrendScoreCalculator, not as a separate signal; the light reads moving-average crosses (ma50/ma200_crossed_*, the observation types that actually exist).\n\nThree conditions are date-based (dividend_ex_date, bmv_holiday, cete_auction) and the last two are marketwide — they carry no asset. The design keeps that distinction visible instead of forcing every rule to pick a ticker.\n\nVendored here: TopBar and BottomNav from the kit; SwitchRow re-vendored 2026-08-27 (two hand-built rows had drifted to a 13px label against the kit's 14 and had lost the row padding — the OFF state on 'Avisos urgentes' was deliberate and survives as an instance override). HeaderBar is LOCAL: Bandeja and Confluencia each hand-built the same back-header, and it is NOT cockpit's TopBarDetail — measured, and they differ in structure (an 18px display title and an optional text action, against a two-line ticker title and a bookmark). Both back buttons were 20px and are 44 now.\n\nPer D4 this flow draws no desktop artboards: its list and sheet are the patterns Holdings and Registrar movimiento already settle.\n\nCopy: es-MX. kit-version-source 0.8.1 (the brief claimed 0.3.0 against a variable reading 0.7.0 — the sixth brief in a row found contradicting its own file, which is what D53 is parked about).",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
